:R-HSA-983189  a            obo:GO_0007018 , owl:NamedIndividual ;
        rdfs:comment        "Kinesins are a superfamily of microtubule-based motor proteins that have diverse functions in transport of vesicles, organelles and chromosomes, and regulate microtubule dynamics. There are 14 families of kinesins, all reprsented in humans. A standardized nomenclature was published in 2004 (Lawrence et al.)." ;
